# MongoDB Animal Shelter Dashboard

## Overview

This project is an interactive animal shelter dashboard built with Python, MongoDB, Dash, JupyterDash, Pandas, Plotly, and Dash Leaflet. It was originally developed in a Jupyter/Codio environment for a database-focused software development course.

The dashboard connects to a MongoDB animal shelter database through a custom Python CRUD module. It allows users to filter animals by rescue type, view matching records in an interactive table, display breed distribution in a pie chart, and view selected animal locations on a map.

## Features

- Connects to a MongoDB database using a custom PyMongo CRUD module
- Reads animal shelter records into a Pandas DataFrame
- Removes MongoDB ObjectId values before displaying data in Dash
- Provides rescue-type filters for:
  - Water Rescue
  - Mountain or Wilderness Rescue
  - Disaster or Individual Tracking
  - Reset
- Displays results in an interactive Dash data table
- Generates a breed distribution pie chart with Plotly
- Displays selected animal location data with Dash Leaflet

## Technologies Used

- Python
- MongoDB
- PyMongo
- Pandas
- Dash
- JupyterDash
- Plotly
- Dash Leaflet

## Project Files

- `ProjectTwoDashboard.ipynb` - Jupyter Notebook containing the dashboard layout, filters, table, chart, and map callbacks
- `CRUD_Python_Module.py` - Python module containing MongoDB CRUD operations for the animal shelter collection

## Environment Note

This project was originally built to run in a Codio/Jupyter environment with access to a local MongoDB animal shelter database. Because the original database and Codio environment are not included in this repository, the project may require additional setup before it can run locally.

Screenshots are included to demonstrate the dashboard output and functionality.

